      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing the dose of Advil without professional guidance is not advisable, even with your current medication. The omeprazole offers protection against acid, but it is not a complete shield against the direct tissue irritation from high-dose NSAIDs. For severe, throbbing tooth pain, a dentist-prescribed topical anesthetic or a stronger, targeted pain reliever is usually the best route. Try to use the lowest effective dose of ibuprofen for the shortest time possible while you await your dental appointment.",
